course: dictionary
lesson: 6735
title: One word, many meanings: olive
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. The word olive can be a fruit, a colour, the oil made from fruit, or a tree. «Greeks sailed in triremes and traded olive oil, wine and pottery.» Here oil tells you that olive means the fruit, and that its oil was traded.
explain: Look for the clue words around the word. In «The dove and the olive branch became symbols of peace», the words symbols of peace show that an olive branch is not a real branch. It is a sign of peace, an offer to stop fighting. Always check: does my meaning fit the sentence?
explain: Colour words can be tricky. «Black mambas are grey or olive-brown.» Olive-brown is a colour, not a fruit, and the word brown next to it is your clue. Olive on its own means a dull yellowish-green colour.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Olive» can mean a small oval fruit, green or black, with a stone inside.
fact: Olive oil is the oil made from olives.
fact: Olive, or olive green, is a dull yellowish-green colour.
fact: An olive tree is the tree that olives grow on.
fact: In stories, «an olive branch» is an offer of peace.
exercise: «Greeks sailed in triremes and traded olive oil, wine and pottery.» What is olive oil? | Paint used on warships | Juice squeezed from lemons | *Oil made from olives
exercise: In the story of Noah, the dove «came back with an olive leaf to show the land was drying». Why did the dove bring back an olive leaf? | To say goodbye to Noah | To show the rain was coming | *To show the land was drying | To ask for food
exercise: «The dove and the olive branch became symbols of peace.» What does an olive branch stand for? | A race between warships | Rain | War | *Peace
test: What colour is olive? | Pure white | Sky blue | Bright red | *Dull yellowish-green
test: What is an olive tree? | A fish found in Greece | A type of snake | *The tree that olives grow on | A kind of warship
exam: «Black mambas are grey or olive-brown.» Which colour is olive-brown most like? | Pure black | Bright pink | *A dull brown with a greenish tinge | Snowy white
